	(text "Switch supply pins (U4-U14 unit B)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 297.18 134.62 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d767aa1a-ab81-420b-bfc5-c618d832fb5c"))
	(text "Reference capacitor: C8 (C0G, +/-0.05 pF) between EXC and CIN through U14.\nSelect it with IO1_5 low and every TX/RX line deselected:\nthe reading is C8 plus board stray. With nothing selected the reading is the zero.\nTwo points = offset and gain check, through the same bus and switch type as a taxel." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 302.26 63.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cd159777-e477-4fcf-8c41-6760e1648f58"))
	(text "TX switches: selected line -> EXC (AD7746 excitation), all others -> GND" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 168.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "256aec63-e922-4103-86c0-027b69638b19"))
	(text "RX switches: selected line -> CIN (AD7746 input), all others -> GND" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 215.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "64cd6c44-42b5-4315-b0ed-435470cf1205"))
	(text "CapScan 5x5: absolute mutual-capacitance scanner for 5 TX x 5 RX printed skin sensors (characterization bench board).\nU2 AD7746 measures the floating capacitance between EXCA and CIN1+: +/-4.096 pF span, CAPDAC offset up to 17 pF, 11-109 ms per conversion, I2C 0x48.\nOne taxel = one TX on EXC, one RX on CIN, the 8 other lines at GND (guarded measurement: the neighbours do not add to the reading).\nU3 PCA9555 (I2C 0x20) drives the 10 select lines. Select is ACTIVE LOW: write 0 to connect a line to its bus. At power-up the PCA9555 pins are inputs\nwith internal 100k pull-ups, so every line sits at GND until the firmware selects one. IO0_0-4 = TX1-5, IO1_0-4 = RX1-5, IO1_5 = reference.\nCIN node budget: about 18 pF (one switch on) + 5 x 6 pF (switches off) + traces + sensor RX-to-GND. AD7746 limit is 60 pF to GND: keep the CIN trace short.\nXIAO: D0 CDC_RDY (low when a conversion is ready), D4 SDA, D5 SCL (default Wire pins), D8 LED_HB, D9 LED_SENSE. USB-C and 3.3 V regulator on the module.\nUnused AD7746 pins (REFIN, VIN, CIN1-, CIN2, EXCB) are left open as allowed by the datasheet (internal reference)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 20.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f29be4c2-bff7-4a8c-bb00-ea24af7d532c"))
	(sheet_instances
    (path "/" (page "1"))
  )
